---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Chrome from "../components/Chrome.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="script.monster Valuation Brief | Premium Domain for Sale | Desert Rich"
  description="A plain brief on the script.monster asking price of $125,000: exact-match keyword, .monster positioning, escrow transfer, and what a buyer should check."
>
  <Chrome>
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14 lg:py-20">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ember">Buyer brief</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.95] sm:text-6xl">How to read a {SITE.askLabel} name</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-muted">
        This is not a market forecast. It is the seller’s framing of one asset: script.monster, offered by {SITE.brand} in {SITE.location}.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">What you are buying</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">The second-level name is the dictionary word script. Six letters, no hyphen, no number. The extension is .monster.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Exact-match names get their price from replacement cost. You pay once so the brand does not pay forever.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">Why {SITE.askLabel}</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">The asking price is published. It is not an auction clock. Offers below the ask are read if they are funded and specific. Buy-now accepts the ask and moves to escrow.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Short category words in software and entertainment clear five and six figures when an end user needs the word itself. That is a pattern, not a promise of appreciation.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">What .monster changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">A matching .com is not the clean word most buyers in this category can get. .monster keeps the keyword and adds a point of view.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">How transfer works</h2>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5">
        <li>You inquire. We reply within one business day.</li>
        <li>Price and terms go into a short written agreement.</li>
        <li>You fund Escrow.com, or another reputable escrow both sides accept.</li>
        <li>The name moves by auth code or registrar push.</li>
        <li>You confirm it is in your account. Escrow releases funds.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">What you should check</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5">
        <li>Trademark search in the classes you will actually use.</li>
        <li>Renewal class at the registry once the name is in your account.</li>
        <li>Social handles. The domain does not include them.</li>
        <li>That your product can live with the tone of the word “monster.”</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col gap-3 border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:flex-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ember" href="/acquire/?intent=buy">Buy now · {SITE.askLabel}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-line" href="/acquire/?intent=offer">Make an offer</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Chrome>
</BaseLayout>
